<p>A driver drove a car into pedestrians on Grimmaische Strasse, a busy shopping street in central Leipzig, Germany, on Monday, killing two people and injuring 22 others, two of them seriously, Reuters reported. Police detained the driver, identified by authorities as a 33-year-old German citizen, and said there was no further danger to the public. Authorities said the motive remained unclear. Leipzig Mayor Burkhard Jung said officials believed the incident was a deliberate rampage. Prosecutors said the suspect was under investigation on suspicion of murder and attempted murder and that they had found no evidence so far linking the attack to political or religious extremism. Mourners gathered near the site Tuesday to lay flowers and candles.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/n00K16VgiYfRvU66Sp7kHk_TZi55dVO5Rz1XZcFObqkj0cmKt0TxUY-YHzs3KIJ6LU68ionCw--H4ZNKtzo6c9mol7mHfvuCDnI3zXAoIhFxbPac-m6aNrBmVmg8HlQsUhnRysPhehtBEEU7W29Vs-69OoQujocqzmEnbIlmgNvd-pEuBknFFZSlqygRvtfR0tFf-V8XxciC8jO_zkluRocYwlRFfK-RcDQUnDinzkzlf4nPSAQ3D-B6UiLPNsrfwE0XbyarXLd6QMI2Gg' alt='Members of the emergency services work at the scene where a car ran into people on a street in the city centre of Leipzig, Germany on Monday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Victims identified: Police and prosecutors identified those killed as a 63-year-old woman and a 77-year-old man, both German citizens.</li><li>Route described: Police Chief René Demmler said the driver drove from Augustusplatz along Grimmaische Strasse into the central pedestrianized shopping area.</li><li>Emergency response: Police, firefighters, emergency medical workers and two helicopters were deployed after the incident.</li><li>Bystander intervention: Witnesses said several bystanders rushed to help victims and restrained the suspect before police arrived.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Leipzig Mayor Burkhard Jung: Jung said he was shocked by the attack and expressed solidarity with victims. (<a href='https://www.infolibre.es